# Arguments for gr8s-server.service; must begin with "serve".
# See `gr8s help serve` for the available options.
#
# --kms-plugin names gr8s-kms (gr8s-kms.service), whose key, sealed to this machine's
# TPM, protects Secrets at rest; --encrypt-secrets-with has a new standalone cluster
# use it from its first Secret. An existing cluster is left as it is: see
# `gr8s help secrets-encrypt` to move one.
GR8S_EXEC_ARGS=serve --state-directory /var/lib/gr8s/server --kms-plugin gr8s=unix:///run/gr8s/kms.sock --encrypt-secrets-with gr8s
